%N A290336 Number of minimal dominating sets in the n-prism graph.
%C A290336 The prism graphs are defined for n>=3. If the sequence is extended to n=1 using P_n X P_2 then a(1)=2 and a(2)=6 (as A290379). The recurrence is the same as that for the Moebius ladder graph (see A290337). - _Andrew Howroyd_, Aug 01 2017
%C A290336 Note that a minimal dominating set has no proper subset be dominating.  It need not have minimum size.  A004524(n+2) is the domination number (size of minimum dominating set) of the n-prism graph.  The largest minimal dominating set of the n-prism has size n. - _Allan Bickle_, Nov 10 2026
%H A290336 Andrew Howroyd, <a href="/A290336/b290336.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 3..200</a>
%H A290336 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/MinimalDominatingSet.html">Minimal Dominating Set</a>.
%H A290336 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/PrismGraph.html">Prism Graph</a>.
%H A290336 <a href="/index/Rec#order_18">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (1,1,2,-1,2,-2,6,4,4,-6,0,-3,5,-1,-2,-5,-2,-2).
%F A290336 a(n) = a(n-1) + a(n-2) + 2*a(n-3) -a(n-4) + 2*a(n-5) - 2*a(n-6) + 6*a(n-7) + 4*a(n-8) + 4*a(n-9) - 6*a(n-10) - 3*a(n-12) + 5*a(n-13) - a(n-14) - 2*a(n-15) - 5*a(n-16) - 2*a(n-17) - 2*a(n-18) for n > 20. - _Andrew Howroyd_, Aug 01 2017
%F A290336 G.f.: x^3*(11 + x + 14*x^2 - 16*x^3 + 44*x^4 + 28*x^5 + 56*x^6 - 52*x^7 - 6*x^8 - 70*x^9 + 52*x^10 - 28*x^11 - 23*x^12 - 97*x^13 - 56*x^14 - 62*x^15 - 12*x^16 - 8*x^17) / ((1 - x)*(1 + 2*x^4 + x^6)*(1 - x^2 - 3*x^3 - 4*x^4 - 4*x^5 - x^6 - 2*x^7 - 3*x^8 - 5*x^9 - 4*x^10 - 2*x^11)). - _Colin Barker_, Aug 02 2017
%e A290336 Mark vertices of a minimal dominating sets with x.  For the 3-prism, there are 6 sets of the first type below, 3 of the second type, and 2 of the third type.  Thus a(3) = 11.
%e A290336    -o-x-o-   -o-x-o-   -x-x-x-
%e A290336    -o-o-x-   -o-x-o-   -o-o-o-
%e A290336 For the 4-prism (cube), there are 4 sets of the first type below, 6 of the second type, and 2 of the third type.  Thus a(4) = 12.
%e A290336    -o-x-o-o-   -o-x-x-o-   -x-o-x-o-
%e A290336    -o-o-o-x-   -o-x-x-o-   -o-x-o-x-
